<?xml version="1.0"?>
<!--
license:BSD-3-Clause
copyright-holders:MAMEdev Team

RC702 display layout — TRUE RC752 (NEC JB-1201M(A)) geometry, 20-unit border.

The RC752 monitor's active display area is 230 x 165 mm (RCSL 44-RT1981) for the
8275's 560 x 275 visible raster (80 cols x 7 dots, 25 rows x 11 lines).  That is
a physical aspect of 230:165 = 46:33 = 1.3939, i.e. pixel aspect ratio 0.685
(pixels ~1.46x taller than wide).  The screen bounds below encode that aspect
exactly (736:528 = 46:33); MAME stretches the square-pixel raster to fill it.

Supersedes the earlier "midpoint PAR" compromise, which averaged square pixels
with a MIS-computed 4:3 target (608x550 = 1.105, not 1.333, and not the real
230:165 = 1.394).  Now driven by the measured physical panel size, not a guess.

Background colour matches rc702_palette pen 0: rgb(0x4F, 0x25, 0x09)
(jbox/RC752 dark warm-brown; was the bright rgb(0xC0,0x60,0x00) orange).
-->
<mamelayout version="2">

	<element name="bg">
		<rect>
			<color red="0.3098" green="0.1451" blue="0.0353" />
		</rect>
	</element>

	<view name="Standard">
		<bounds x="0" y="0" width="776" height="568" />
		<element ref="bg">
			<bounds x="0" y="0" width="776" height="568" />
		</element>
		<screen index="0">
			<bounds x="20" y="20" width="736" height="528" />
		</screen>
	</view>

</mamelayout>
